the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the Jahreseinkommen of *a case* is *a number*; scenario element.
    Einkommensprüfung holds for *a case*.
    Einkommensprüfung would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r4_8_income_check_with_text_and_actions includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/income-check-with-text-and-actions.ruml".

sgb ii 11 is published at "/akn/de/act/2003-12-24/sgb-2#sec_11".

rule node_1 with provenance sgb ii 11:
Einkommensprüfung holds for a case if
    the Jahreseinkommen of the case is a number N
    and N > 50000.

Einkommensprüfung holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Jahreseinkommen of the case is a number
    and Einkommensprüfung would hold for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "income-check-with-text-and-actions.ruml" at generated_1:
    % every data point its first value
    the Jahreseinkommen of case 1 is 50000.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Einkommensprüfung holds for case 1"].

scenario generated_2 is, as stated in "income-check-with-text-and-actions.ruml" at generated_2:
    % dp_annual_income has no value
    node_1 expects answers ["Einkommensprüfung holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Einkommensprüfung holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

scenario generated_3 is, as stated in "income-check-with-text-and-actions.ruml" at generated_3:
    % dp_annual_income is 49999
    the Jahreseinkommen of case 1 is 49999.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Einkommensprüfung holds for case 1"].

scenario generated_4 is, as stated in "income-check-with-text-and-actions.ruml" at generated_4:
    % dp_annual_income is 50001
    the Jahreseinkommen of case 1 is 50001.
    node_1 expects answers ["Einkommensprüfung holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers [].

query node_1 is:
    Einkommensprüfung holds for case 1.

query not_node_1 is:
    it is not the case that Einkommensprüfung holds for case 1.

